"## Summary\n\nIsolation follow-up 26: the operator assist's capacity write moves onto the shared bounded node-write helper, with an offline proof, and D-162's reach into the harness's configs is audited. Offline only.\n- **Session:** launched 11:48 EST on 2026-11-04 on #478's roadmap row (`df61fd68`).\n  - The first session ended at 12:05 on a model service error, \"Selected model is at capacity\", while it waited for host admission to run its last gate. Its first three commits were done and its tree was clean.\n  - The orchestrator resumed the same conversation at 12:07. It ran the committed-evidence hygiene test, finalized its records and delivered at 12:54.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 4 commits and 16 owned files, +1,229/−25. Most of it is the dated document and the validation records under `history/follow-up-26-validation/`.\n  - **The code:**\n    - `assist.go.txt`, the assist's Go text, now a committed file;\n    - `assist_offline_test.go.txt`, the fake-server suite;\n    - `assist.py` and `driver.py`, which overlay them;\n    - `driver_writes_test.go` and `mk/at-isolation.mk`.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: current `main` (`8f4374d3`, after handover 47, #479) with this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/at-isolation.mk at-isolation-lint`, `at-isolation-test` and `at-isolation-build`. The test target now runs the offline assist suite: all five cases pass;\n    - `make -f mk/e2e.mk e2e-lint`;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...`;\n    - the committed-evidence tests (`TestCommitted*` in `tests/netlab`, `tests/e2e` and `tests/e2e/at/...`);\n    - `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** no Docker, no lab, no stack, no assembled run and no reservation. The assist was never run live.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The assist's write** (`127bbe3f`). The PATCH formerly at `assist.py:22` now lives in `assist.go.txt`. The live entry point and the offline suite call the same function.\n  - It calls the shared `writeNode` with `nodeFieldsMatch` on one capacity body, the way the driver's capacity writes do. The initial GET's ETag is its first `If-Match`. The helper is unchanged.\n  - **The evidence keeps the helper's receipt** under `node_write`, with every attempt and every reread.\n  - **`api_ok` is corrected.** It now means the helper accepted the command, already-intended fields included. Before, it was true for any reply without a transport error, a 412 or a 500 included. It is still not an observed-state result.\n  - **Unchanged:** the capacity values, the action text, the address and route restore, and `assisted: true`.\n- **The offline proof** (`481db864`). Five fake-server cases, with no Docker and no lab:\n  - a direct 202;\n  - an exact `RESOURCE_VERSION_CONFLICT`, a reread, then a 202: two attempts with one idempotency key and one body, both in the evidence. A reread showing only part of the desired capacity does not count as intended;\n  - an HTTP 500, and a 412 with another code: one attempt each, no retry, and `api_ok` false;\n  - a reread that already shows the complete desired capacity: already intended, with `http_status` left at 412.\n  - **An AST check** confirms that `assist.go.txt` makes exactly one node write and no bypass. The lane's lint now covers every `*.go.txt`.\n- **D-162's reach** (`5c86dc5f`), for every routed line and every config the harness writes or inherits:\n  - the main agent's runtime stays 1 s for heartbeat, poll and observation, before and after D-162, through the observer's override;\n  - the boot-release auxiliary config and the clone's runtime inherit that 1 s;\n  - only the enrollment files carry D-162's 5 s.\n  - No coherent-window, sample or incident check changed.\n- **Request to devstack:** review the shared second-exit clone's receiver wiring. The clone copies the source's control URL, port 9445, where isolation's observer listens on the source. But it starts the original image, whose helper proxy listens on 9444. This is a static concern only, with no measured failure and no re-score.\n- **Carried:** AT11's and AT13's operator matrices, and F17-01 under D-163. Every historical failure stays failed.\n"
